WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.360
Believe it or not, the Sonic the Hedgehog
movie is finally on the way.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.600
If you want to know more details about the
film, then you've come to the right place.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.620
This is everything we know about the Blue
Blur's big screen debut, and why you should

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.680
be looking forward to it.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.580
Sonic the Hedgehog was already supposed to
be upon us.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.080
The film has been in development since 2013,
but the production really ramped up in 2017

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:24.580
and 2018.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:30.040
The original release was scheduled for November
8, 2019, but the first trailer in April of

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:35.670
2019 caused such a negative reaction - particularly
to the title character's design - that the

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.160
studio pulled the film back to work on some
alterations.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:43.640
However, it appears the redesigned film is
finally up to snuff, as the new release date

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.300
of February 14, 2020 seems like it is set
in stone.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:52.220
If your idea of a romantic Valentine's Day
date is with a blue anthropomorphic hedgehog

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:55.120
wearing sneakers, then you are in luck in
2020.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:00.600
After the controversy that swirled around
the original trailer, the reworked version

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:05.530
released in November of 2019 has received
much more praise for being faithful to the

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.600
tone of the franchise.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.780
It does a decent job of setting the stage:
Sonic - voiced by Ben Schwartz - is a lonely

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.920
alien who lives on Earth and is bored out
of his mind.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:20.100
After he causes a huge power surge, several
forces start converging to try to capture

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:25.080
Sonic and harness his powers, which he tells
us could let them "conquer the universe."

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.320
One of those forces is Jim Carrey's Dr. Robotnik.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.820
"Give me a BIG, FAT BREAK!"

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.260
Otherwise, the trailer shows a lot of references
to Sonic video games, showcases the film's

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.060
sense of humor, and focuses on two central
things: Robotnik's weapons and the friendship

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.960
between Sonic and Tom - played by James Marsden.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:49.840
It seems like a pretty strong showcase of
the movie's tone, so you'll have a good idea

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:53.940
what you're getting into before you decide
if you want to see Sonic the Hedgehog.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.200
The director of Sonic the Hedgehog, Jeff Fowler,
has an interesting pedigree.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.800
He's been nominated for an Oscar, albeit in
the category for "Best Animated Short."

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.099
That nomination - shared with Deadpool and
Terminator: Dark Fate director Tim Miller

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:13.310
- comes courtesy of his time in the director's
chair for the 2004 film Gopher Broke.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.560
Otherwise... that's it.

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:19.780
Yes, Fowler only has one directorial credit
to his name, and it's an animated short film

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.040
from over a decade ago.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.860
That's potentially a bit disheartening.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.099
Of course, Fowler has worked on a few different
films in different departments, including

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.340
a stint on the visual effects team for Where
the Wild Things Are.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:35.620
Sonic's screenplay credit is shared among
Josh Miller, Patrick Casey, and Oren Uziel.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:40.319
The first two worked together writing films
like Transylmania and Dorm Daze.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.620
Uziel's portfolio includes contributions to
22 Jump Street and The Cloverfield Paradox.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.080
Essentially, it's an eclectic combination
of writing experience and untested directorial

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:53.620
talent that will hopefully come together to
make something fun with Sonic the Hedgehog.

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:59.379
There aren't a ton of details about the actual
plot of the Sonic the Hedgehog film, but here's

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.000
what we know.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.980
The official synopsis reads: "Sonic tries
to navigate the complexities of life on Earth

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.840
with his newfound best friend - a human named
Tom Wachowski.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:14.260
They must soon join forces to prevent the
evil Dr. Robotnik from capturing Sonic and

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.260
using his powers for world domination."

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.900
So, we know Sonic is an alien who teams up
with James Marsden's character.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.780
He can apparently use the golden rings as
teleportation portals, as the film's trailer

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.280
shows him doing this a few times.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:31.959
And we know Dr. Robotnik wants to capture
Sonic to harness his powers and use them for

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.400
his own personal gain.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:38.079
The tone and general plot beats we've seen
in the trailer showcase the film as being

00:03:38.079 --> 00:03:41.829
a bit of an oddball buddy film with some slapstick
action thrown in.

00:03:41.829 --> 00:03:46.360
It will be interesting to see how much explanation
the film offers of Sonic and his abilities.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:51.200
Maybe it will just say something to the effect
of, "Well, he's a super powerful alien.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:52.240
What more do you need?"

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.660
"How are you not dead?"

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.500
"I have no idea!"

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.579
Let's talk about the hedgehog in the room:
the reaction to the first Sonic the Hedgehog

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.640
trailer was loud and angry.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:08.220
Our hero was originally made to look considerably
more... realistic than the version we're getting.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.040
Well, as realistic as a humanoid cartoon hedgehog
can look.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.000
It… did not work.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.740
The off-putting design, coupled with the "trying
too hard" punchlines, caused a massive outcry

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:20.620
from fans.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.480
Sonic was mocked relentlessly, and the studio
actually listened.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.560
Director Jeff Fowler took to Twitter to reassure
fans that Sega and Paramount got the message,

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.480
quote, "loud and clear," punctuating the promise
with the hashtag "#gottafixfast."

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.820
And fix it fast they did.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.660
The film was delayed as the team went back
to the drawing board with Sonic's design,

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.880
reportedly costing the production an extra
$5 million.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.340
It actually seemed to work.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:50.180
Upon release of the official "redesigned"
trailer, fan reaction was almost the complete

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.740
opposite of the first time around.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:56.440
The redesigned Sonic actually resembled the
character that fans loved, and the response

00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:58.560
to the trailer was extremely positive.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.060
You see?

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.960
Fans on the internet sometimes can bring about
good change!

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:06.639
Of course, in the movie business, a happy
ending sometimes hides a grim story.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:11.229
Despite some skepticism, it seems like the
crew of the Sonic movie pulled off the mighty

00:05:11.229 --> 00:05:16.410
task of redesigning their main character and
starting over from scratch on no small number

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.570
of completed visual effects sequences.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:23.379
MPC Vancouver, the studio that redesigned
the character, was promptly rewarded for their

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.770
efforts by… being shut down.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:30.200
That's a pretty steep price to pay for Sonic's
teeth to not induce nightmares.

